index 02a2c8c..da44fda 100644
--- a/docs/sme/live-history-cli.md
+++ b/docs/sme/live-history-cli.md
@@ -56,6 +56,31 @@ Host, physical devices, other callback configurations, and arbitrary concurrent
 UI callers are outside this scope. Native Stop is not a restart facility: a later
 Play can be rejected, and that genuine result belongs in the transcript.
 
+## Explicit admission policy
+
+Both commands accept `--admission native_attempt|ordered_job_scans`; omission
+preserves the existing `native_attempt` behavior. The selected policy is logged
+before file/owner work and included in successful JSON reports.
+
+- `native_attempt` admits fully represented job-scan/publication overlaps for one
+  real strict comparison attempt. It does not recover their atomic order, and
+  the attempt may fail with a genuine mismatch.
+- `ordered_job_scans` rejects the two known same-slot selector-predicate overlaps
+  with `CrossedScan`: Worker scan versus Control queued publication, and Control
+  acceptance scan versus Worker completed publication. It retains every other
+  preflight check and actual comparison. It is a restricted admission subset,
+  not a universal replay guarantee or a scheduler that chooses expected results.
+
+For example, add `--admission ordered_job_scans` to both invocations above.
+Record uses the policy in full readback validation after genuine teardown and
+framing seal, before publication/rename. On rejection, the `.incomplete` file is
+not published, even if its framing is sealed. Replay applies the policy before
+Session/Host creation. There is no automatic fallback, recapture, or retry to
+find a passing interleaving. A negative pre-owner rejection is not native replay
+success. The policy is not embedded in the tape and changes neither profile 9 /
+wire 2 nor executable/bank/config/source identity checks; select it explicitly
+again on replay. Legacy API wrappers and default CLI operation remain unchanged.
+
 ## Script semantics
 
 A script is an object with `auto_events` (default true) and an ordered `actions`
diff --git a/docs/sme/live-semantic-profile.md b/docs/sme/live-semantic-profile.md
index cab0c0b..770ec86 100644
--- a/docs/sme/live-semantic-profile.md
+++ b/docs/sme/live-semantic-profile.md
@@ -72,6 +72,27 @@ ambiguities remain unsupported. Replay never searches alternative event orders,
 retries to fit expected outcomes, or supplies an expected result. Only explicit
 offline execution may wait at a semantic cut.
 
+The explicit admission policies are `native_attempt` (the compatible default)
+and `ordered_job_scans`. `validateInputsWithPolicy` and `Driver.initWithPolicy`
+select the policy; their existing wrappers retain `native_attempt`.
+`ordered_job_scans` runs the same complete preflight, but rejects same-slot
+Worker-read/Control-queued and Control-read/Worker-completed bracket overlaps
+with `CrossedScan`, before Session or Host creation. These are the two cross-role
+stores that change the respective `state == queued` / `state == completed`
+selector predicates. Running and free transitions do not change the opposing
+selector predicate, including failed/cancelled jobs that still pass through
+completed before free.
+
+This is a narrower admitted subset, not a new atomic scheduler or a promise
+that all native comparisons will succeed. A preserved attempt-mode mismatch
+remains a failed attempt; rejecting that same tape under the ordered policy is
+only pre-owner rejection evidence, not successful replay. Policy is an explicit
+caller option, not a wire field: profile 9 / wire 2 and all same-build identity
+checks remain unchanged. A tape does not attest which policy published it;
+replay must select and revalidate the desired policy. Recorder sealing remains
+framing-only. File publication follows separate full readback admission; ordered
+rejection leaves the recording unpublished rather than relabeling its bytes.
+
 Poisoning suppresses later playback invocations but does not authorize freeing.
 Real callback stop/join, Worker park/ack/stop/join, native destruction and source
 release still run. If native cleanup cannot complete, retained resources remain
